-- 2990_r48_academy_guides.sql
-- Release 48 in the academy (docs/changes/2026-11-14-r48-academy-guides.md). The owner (Nov 14): staff keep asking things
-- the guides already answer, and staff help renters, so they must know the renter portal and the renter guide.
--   1. One section of worked examples per role (customer service, Sales in person and remote, Fleet, Finance, field work,
--      Admin), written from that role's guide chapters: what the renter or a colleague says, where to click, what to say,
--      with the guide's screenshots. Each ends with its quiz, drawn from the examples.
--   2. A new shared path, The renter's side (renter_side), for every staff role: one section per step of the renter guide
--      (request, offer, details and signing, paying and the deposit, coverage proof with the pink slip and OPCF 27, pickup,
--      the trip, the return and the deposit back, common errors), each showing what the renter sees and linking to the page.
--      app.academy_paths_of gives it to everyone who has a path, so one-step Hire enrolls new hires on it from the start
--      (app.academy_enroll) and the onboarding gate holds them until it is passed, as for every path.
--   3. Staff already working who had passed everything get 7 days (their gated enrollments' lock_from, the date the
--      academy page shows) before the new sections hold them; staff not done yet are held as before. Nothing is reset.
--   4. A scene can show a guide screenshot (kind shot: the chapter, the image, a line): the lesson check accepts it.
